{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.barOddPhase_eq_moment_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.barOddPhase_eq_moment_form","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.lean#L262-L284","doc":"**The unique bar-odd eigenphase is `([2]_q·Ξ − 2)·h/2`.**\n\n`QOU.QBeta.loopMean_eq_twoQ_mul_moment` gives `2z − h = [2]_q·Ξ` in ANY\nconvention, with `Ξ = Σ_λ χ^λ(τ)·y_λ` the transposition moment of the\nWedderburn weights (n-independent, and bar-even under D because every\nconvention-D weight is — `markovWeightsD_y21_barEven`).\n\nCombining with §2: the bar-even half of the Markov parameter is `[2]_q·Ξ/2`\nand its bar-odd half is the universal `h/2`.  So the bar-odd projection of\nthe eigenphase is determined by the weights, even though — per\n`no_weight_function_gives_phase` — the full phase is not.\n\nStated division-free in the doubled phase: `2·α^odd = (2z − h − 2)·h/2 · 2`,\ni.e. `(2z − h − 2)·h`, so no inverse of `2` is needed and the identity holds\nover any `CommRing`.\n\nThis is the sense in which the D-frame eigenphase is RE-DERIVED rather than\nsubstituted: its bar-even multiplier comes from the D weights, and its\nbar-odd factor is the `h` those weights cannot supply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.zD_even_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.zD_even_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.lean#L247-L258","doc":"**`z_D − h/2` is bar-EVEN**, division-free: with `q⁻¹` carried as `qi`\n(`q·qi = 1`), the cross-multiplied form of\n`(qi⁴+1)/(2·qi·(qi²+1)) = (q⁴+1)/(2·q·(q²+1))`.\n\nThis is what makes the shifted parameter a legitimate eigenphase source:\na bar-even parameter yields a bar-odd phase by\n`QOU.QBeta.eigenphase_barOdd_of_barEven`, which is exactly the property the\nC frame had for free and the naive D substitution loses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.zD_sub_halfH_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.zD_sub_halfH_eq","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.lean#L239-L245","doc":"**`z_D − h/2 = (q⁴ + 1) / (2q(q² + 1))`.**  The closed form of the unique\nbar-odd parameter under convention D.  Stated over a field with the two\nnonvanishing hypotheses made explicit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.barOdd_forces_oddPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.barOdd_forces_oddPart","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.lean#L215-L235","doc":"**Bar-oddness forces the shift's bar-odd part to be `−h/2`, and nothing\nelse.**  The forward direction is the pruning; the reverse direction shows\nit holds for EVERY bar-even `ce`, which is the non-uniqueness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.generalShift_bar_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.generalShift_bar_defect","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.lean#L195-L213","doc":"**The defect of a general shift depends only on the shift's bar-ODD part.**\n\nSplit the shift as `c = ce + co` with `bar ce = ce` and `bar co = −co`.\nThen\n\n    bar(2α_c) + 2α_c = h·(h + 2·co),\n\nwith `ce` absent — and `z` absent too. So the bar-even half of the shift is\ninvisible to the involution and parity constrains only `co`.\n\nThis is the statement that makes `barOdd_shift_unique` a *narrower* result\nthan it looks: within `h`-proportional shifts the answer is a single `t`,\nbut among all shifts the answer is an affine family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.barOdd_parameter_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.barOdd_parameter_eq","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.lean#L184-L191","doc":"**The unique bar-odd parameter is `z − h/2`.**  Restating\n`barOdd_shift_unique` in terms of the parameter rather than the shift: the\nsurviving member of the family is the bar-EVEN projection of `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.barOdd_shift_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.barOdd_shift_unique","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.lean#L162-L182","doc":"**Bar-oddness holds iff `t = −1/2`.**  The shift that restores the parity\nevery downstream consumer assumes is unique, and it is a pure number: no\ndependence on `q`, on the anchor, or on which full-bar parameter one\nstarted from.  This is the pruning step — the hypothesis class of D-frame\neigenphases `α_t` collapses to a single member before any number is\ncomputed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.naivePhase_not_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.naivePhase_not_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.lean#L134-L146","doc":"**The bare substitution is never bar-odd.**  At `t = 0` — that is, using\n`z_D` itself in the C-frame formula — the defect is `h²`, which is nonzero\naway from the classical point.  Together with\n`QOU.QBeta.decayLadder_zC_threeRow_ne_zero` (which blocks the same move from\nthe Temperley–Lieb side) this is why the convention change is a\nre-derivation and not a `z`-swap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.shiftedPhase_bar_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.shiftedPhase_bar_defect","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameEigenphaseBarOdd.lean#L117-L132","doc":"**The bar defect of the shifted eigenphase is `(2t + 1)·h²`.**\n\nWith the parameter shifted to `z + t·h` (`t` bar-even), the doubled phase is\n`2α_t = (z + t·h − 1)·h`, whose bar-image is `(bar z + t·bar h − 1)·bar h`.\nFeeding the full-bar condition `bar z = z − h` and `bar h = −h`:\n\n    bar(2α_t) + 2α_t = (2t + 1)·h².\n\nTwo things about the right-hand side carry the content. It does not mention\n`z` — so the defect is a property of the *whole* full-bar family, and no\nchoice of parameter within that family can change it. And it is not\nidentically zero — so bar-oddness is a genuine constraint on `t`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}